National formats (schema layer only)
------------------------------------
The XSDs below are the issuing authorities' own schemas. They are vendored byte-for-byte except where a
bundle's manifest lists `modifiedFiles`: there the remote `schemaLocation` of an imported schema (the W3C
XML Signature schema, the Polish common types) is rewritten to the vendored copy so nothing is fetched at
runtime. The manifest records the SHA-256 of every downloaded original under `source`. Most of these
files carry no licence text. They are published by the authorities for implementers to validate documents
against, and vendoring them for that purpose is the same practice as the KoSIT and OpenPEPPOL
configurations. If a rights holder objects, the bundle is removed from build-validation-bundles.ts and from
planFor(); nothing else depends on it. Release dates marked "vendoring date" in a manifest mean the
schema states none; they are the day the file was copied (2026-10-16).

