Not bundled: Peppol PINT and ZATCA rules
========================================

The Peppol PINT Schematron (PINT, PINT SG, A-NZ, JP, MY, AE, OM, EU), its code lists and its examples are
published at https://docs.peppol.eu/poac under an OpenPEPPOL copyright statement that says the document "may
not be modified, re-distribute, sold or repackaged in any other way without the prior consent of OpenPEPPOL
AISBL". That does not allow pinning copies here, so PINT documents get the UBL 2.1 XSD layer only and the
profile layer reports 'not-run'. Add the bundles (build-validation-bundles.ts handles a Schematron given as
.sch or .xslt) if OpenPEPPOL's consent is obtained. The same goes for ZATCA's Schematron and SDK samples.
